/* ==================== Script 788 id="amiyo-imp2-02" ==================== */
/* Import 2, step 2/20 (step139): Interpret footage, like Premiere's right-click > Modify > Interpret Footage, plus a shared badge row on media cards.
   ⋯ More > "Interpret footage…": tell the editor to play a file at a different frame rate. A 60 fps clip played as 24 fps becomes smooth 2.5x slow motion;
   a 24 fps clip played as 30 fps runs a little faster. Quick buttons for 24 / 25 / 30 / 50 / 60, or type any speed. New clips of that file come in already conformed.
   You can also apply it to clips already on the timeline (they stay in order: later clips move to make room). The card shows a "⏱ plays as 24 fps" badge. One Undo step. */
